  "purpose": "measure, inside the TRAIN split, how much of the unseen-task test gap is attributable to task identity (leave-one-task-out).",
  "decision_rule_preregistered": "claim: the LOTO gap is the fraction of the unseen-task gap explained by task identity; frac = (mean_auc_in_sample_reference - mean_auc_loto) / (mean_auc_in_sample_reference - 0.8220322044197129). Evaluated only if the denominator is positive (> 0); otherwise the fraction is recorded as null with reason 'denominator <= 0: in-sample reference is not above the published test AUC, so no optimism/gap can be apportioned'. mean_auc_in_sample_reference is matched to the LOTO evaluation sets: one model trained on all train records, then scored separately on each held-out class's windows, and averaged over exactly the classes used in mean_auc_loto. Pre-registered BEFORE any model in this script was trained.",
